@model DimensionRecordEditViewModel
@*
    One record's names and attributes.

    Moving it is not here. A move changes what every historical report under the unit resolves to,
    which is why it has its own permission, its own dry run and its own dated form in the designer;
    this links to that one rather than being a second way to do the one thing that most needs one
    way. Retiring is the same argument.
*@
<h1 id="record-edit-heading">@T["Edit {0}", Model.CurrentNameEn]</h1>

<p class="text-muted">
    <code>@Model.Code</code>
    <span>@T["A {0}. The code is the natural key and cannot change.", Model.TypeName]</span>
</p>

<div asp-validation-summary="All" class="text-danger mb-3"></div>

<form method="post" asp-action="Edit" asp-route-id="@Model.RecordId" id="record-edit">
    <input type="hidden" asp-for="RecordId" />

    <workmate-bilingual for-en="NameEn" for-ar="NameAr" label="@T["Name"]" required="true" max-length="200" />

    <div class="mb-3" style="max-width: 16rem;">
        <label class="form-label" asp-for="EffectiveFrom">@T["Name effective from"]</label>
        <input class="form-control" type="date" asp-for="EffectiveFrom" required />
        <span asp-validation-for="EffectiveFrom" class="text-danger"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="form-check mb-3">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" asp-for="IsCorrection" id="record-edit-correction" />
        <label class="form-check-label" asp-for="IsCorrection">@T["This is a correction: the old text was always wrong"]</label>
        @* The two kinds answer "what was this called last March" differently, and nothing
           downstream can infer which was meant. A substantive rename starts a new dated period and
           leaves prior ones alone; a correction rewrites the period that already covers the date,
           which is what a typo found by running last year's report needs. *@
        <div class="form-text">
            @T["Left unticked, the unit genuinely became something else on the date above and earlier periods keep the old name. Ticked, the new name replaces the old one for the period that covers that date."]
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Below the dated rename block on purpose: everything above it is about the name's history and
       none of it applies here. An alias has no periods, so there is no date to apply it from and no
       question about which kind of change is meant — it simply is what it is from now on. *@
    @{ var aliasHint = T["Optional. Shown beside the name on this dimension's list and tree. Not dated: changing it changes what every report shows, including past ones."].Value; }
    <workmate-bilingual for-en="AliasEn" for-ar="AliasAr" label="@T["Alias"]"
                        hint="@aliasHint" max-length="255" />

    @* A position's grades are here where its parent is not, and the difference is what each does to
       history: changing a parent rewrites what every historical report under the unit resolves to,
       which is why it is a dated move with its own permission and its own dry run below. Changing
       which grades a post offers is ordinary record upkeep that no past report resolves through —
       the same line the alias above is on. D26 C.

       Who it reports to is a parent too, on the reporting-line axis (ADR-0028), so it is in the
       "Where it sits" table below with its own Move button rather than being a box here. *@
    @if (Model.IsPosition)
    {
        @* ---- Reports to: shown, not edited. Decision D31. ---------------------------------

            REPORTS TO IS A PARENT, on the reporting-line axis. Changing a parent rewrites what
            every report resolves to, which is why it is a dated move with its own permission and
            its own dry run — the same reason the organisation parent is not on this form either.
            So this says what is true and links to where that move lives.

            The third state is the one worth having: a position that is on the reporting line
            NOWHERE. Every post created through the old screen with Reports to left blank got
            exactly that, silently, and D31 is what stops it happening again.
        *@
        <h2 class="fs-5 mt-4">@T["Reporting line"]</h2>

        <dl class="row mb-3" id="record-edit-reports-to">
            <dt class="col-sm-3">@T["Reports to"]</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9">
                @if (!Model.IsOnTheReportingLine)
                {
                    <span class="text-warning" id="record-edit-not-on-reporting-line">
                        @T["This position is not on the reporting line at all, so nothing below it answers to it. Put it on the line to fix that."]
                    </span>
                }
                else if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.ReportsToName))
                {
                    <span id="record-edit-reports-to-top">@T["Nobody — this is the top of the reporting line."]</span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span id="record-edit-reports-to-name">@Model.ReportsToName</span>
                }

                @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.ReportingStructureId))
                {
                    <div class="form-text">
                        @T["Changing this moves the post to another part of the reporting line, which is a dated change with its own permission."]
                        <a id="record-edit-reporting-line-link"
                           asp-controller="OrganisationDesignerAdmin" asp-action="Index"
                           asp-route-structureId="@Model.ReportingStructureId">@T["Open the reporting line"]</a>
                    </div>
                }
            </dd>
        </dl>

        <h2 class="fs-5 mt-4">@T["Grades"]</h2>

        @* A checklist with nothing ticked posts nothing at all, so without this "clear every grade"
           and "this form never asked about grades" arrive identically. The empty value is filtered
           out before the write; what it carries is the fact that the question was asked. *@
        <input type="hidden" name="AllowedGradeRecordIds" value="" />

        var gradesHint = T["The levels of this post. Removing one never changes the grade of anybody already on it — it stops being offered."].Value;

        <workmate-grade-picker for="AllowedGradeRecordIds" label="@T["Allowed grades"]"
                               multiple="true"
                               hint="@gradesHint" />
    }

    @if (Model.Attributes.Count > 0)
    {
        <h2 class="fs-5 mt-4">@T["Details"]</h2>
        <p class="text-muted small">@T["Defined on this kind of unit in the Dimension types screen."]</p>
    }

    @foreach (var index in Enumerable.Range(0, Model.Attributes.Count))
    {
        <partial name="_UnitAttribute" model="Model.Attributes[index]"
                 view-data="@(new ViewDataDictionary(ViewData)
                     { TemplateInfo = { HtmlFieldPrefix = $"Attributes[{index}]" } })" />
    }

    <div class="mt-4">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" id="record-edit-submit">@T["Save"]</button>
        <a class="btn btn-link" asp-action="Index"
           asp-route-dimensionTypeId="@Model.DimensionTypeId"
           asp-route-structureId="@Model.StructureId">@T["Cancel"]</a>
    </div>
</form>

<h2 class="fs-5 mt-4">@T["Where it sits"]</h2>

<table class="table table-sm" id="record-edit-placements">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>@T["Structure"]</th>
            <th>@T["Parent"]</th>
            <th class="text-end">@T["Actions"]</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        @foreach (var placement in Model.Placements)
        {
            <tr class="record-edit-placement" data-structure-id="@placement.StructureId">
                <td>@placement.StructureName</td>
                <td>
                    @if (placement.State == DimensionRecordPlacementState.Placed)
                    {
                        <span>@placement.Path</span>
                    }
                    else if (placement.State == DimensionRecordPlacementState.TopLevel)
                    {
                        <span class="text-muted">@T["Top level"]</span>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <span class="text-warning">@T["Not placed"]</span>
                    }
                </td>
                <td class="text-end">
                    @* The designer's own dated screens. A move is refused, previewed and audited
                       there; doing it here would be a second mechanism for the operation that can
                       least afford one. *@
                    <div class="btn-group btn-group-sm">
                        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary record-edit-move"
                           asp-controller="OrganisationDesignerAdmin" asp-action="Move"
                           asp-route-structureId="@placement.StructureId"
                           asp-route-recordId="@Model.RecordId">@T["Move…"]</a>
                        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary record-edit-retire"
                           asp-controller="OrganisationDesignerAdmin" asp-action="Retire"
                           asp-route-structureId="@placement.StructureId"
                           asp-route-recordId="@Model.RecordId">@T["Retire…"]</a>
                    </div>
                </td>
            </tr>
        }
    </tbody>
</table>

@if (Model.IsPosition)
{
    @* The allowed-grades checklist's search box and live count. The checkboxes themselves work
       without it — see GradePickerTagHelper. *@
    <script asp-name="workmate-grade-picker" at="Foot"></script>
}
